---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial | Ipsita CRTX"
  description="Recurring editorial systems spanning internal communication, content curation, copy development and brand storytelling."
>
  <Header active="work" />

  <main class="newsletter-page">

    <!-- =====================================================
         HERO
    ====================================================== -->

    <section class="newsletter-hero shell">

      <a
        class="newsletter-back"
        href="/work/content-strategy"
      >
        ← Content Strategy
      </a>

      <p class="eyebrow">
        Content Strategy / Editorial System
      </p>

      <div class="newsletter-hero__grid">

        <div class="newsletter-hero__copy">

          <h1 class="display">
            Editorial &<br />
            <span>Newsletter Systems.</span>
          </h1>

          <p class="newsletter-hero__lead">
            I build editorial systems around what the audience needs to notice, understand and remember.


          </p>

          <p class="newsletter-hero__intro">
            My process is to identify the strongest stories, establish hierarchy, compress complex
            information without stripping away context, and create a consistent structure that can adapt
            as the content changes.
          </p>

          <div class="newsletter-tags">
            <span>Editorial Strategy</span>
            <span>Content Curation</span>
            <span>Copy Development</span>
            <span>Information Hierarchy</span>
            <span>Visual Systems</span>
          </div>

        </div>


        <div class="newsletter-hero__visual">

          <div class="newsletter-hero-collage">

            <img
              class="newsletter-hero-collage__main"
              src="/images/newsletters/hero1.webp"
              alt="Newsletter editorial work"
            />

            <img
              src="/images/newsletters/hero2.webp"
              alt="Schneider Electric newsletter"
            />

            <img
              src="/images/newsletters/hero3.webp"
              alt="CynLr newsletter concept"
            />

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>



    <!-- =====================================================
         01 — TWO SYSTEMS
    ====================================================== -->

    <section class="newsletter-section shell">

      <div class="section-heading">

        <p class="eyebrow">
          01 / Two Editorial Systems
        </p>

        <div class="section-rule">
          <span>⌁</span>
        </div>

      </div>


      <div class="newsletter-section__intro">

        <h2 class="display">
          One discipline.<br />
          <span>Two Contexts.</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          The Schneider Electric newsletters demonstrate the ability to sustain
          a recurring editorial system over time. The CynLr work explores how
          an editorial concept can be built from a blank strategic brief.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="newsletter-comparison">

        <article>

          <span class="newsletter-comparison__index">01</span>

          <p class="newsletter-kicker">
            Schneider Electric
          </p>

          <h3 class="display">
            Recurring Systems.
          </h3>

          <p>
            Multiple editions produced from changing monthly inputs while
            maintaining a consistent information and visual system.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Recurring production</li>
            <li>Multiple stakeholder inputs</li>
            <li>High-volume content selection</li>
            <li>Internal distribution</li>
          </ul>

        </article>


        <article>

          <span class="newsletter-comparison__index">02</span>

          <p class="newsletter-kicker">
            CynLr
          </p>

          <h3 class="display">
            Editorial exploration.
          </h3>

          <p>
            Four newsletter concepts developed as part of a content strategy
            problem statement, with greater emphasis on editorial voice,
            narrative and strategic framing.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Editorial concept development</li>
            <li>Brand voice</li>
            <li>Content pillars</li>
            <li>Narrative structure</li>
          </ul>

        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="newsletter-system-ctas">

      <a
        href="#schneider-newsletters"
        class="newsletter-system-cta"
      >
        <span>01</span>

        <div>
          <small>Explore system</small>
          <strong>Schneider Electric</strong>
        </div>

        <i aria-hidden="true">↓</i>
      </a>


      <a
        href="#cynlr-newsletters"
        class="newsletter-system-cta"
      >
        <span>02</span>

        <div>
          <small>Explore system</small>
          <strong>CynLr</strong>
        </div>

        <i aria-hidden="true">↓</i>
      </a>

    </div>

    </section>



    <!-- =====================================================
         02 — SCHNEIDER SYSTEM
    ====================================================== -->

    <section class="newsletter-section shell" id="schneider-newsletters">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        Schneider Electric
      </p>

      <div class="section-rule">
        <span>⌁</span>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="newsletter-section__intro">

      <h2 class="display">
        Editorial evolution<br />
        <span>across recurring issues.</span>
      </h2>

      <p>
        The system evolved from open, modular editorial compositions toward a
        denser and more structured visual language as the volume and complexity
        of lab communication increased.
      </p>

    </div>

    <!-- =====================================================
        2026
    ====================================================== -->

    <div class="newsletter-archive-year">

      <div class="newsletter-archive-year__heading">
        <span>02</span>

        <div>
          <p class="newsletter-kicker">
            Evolved editorial system
          </p>

          <h3 class="display">
            2026
          </h3>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div class="newsletter-masonry">

        {
          newsletterIssues2026.map((issue) => (

            <button
              class:list={[
                'newsletter-masonry-item',
                {
                  'newsletter-masonry-item--special':
                    issue.special,
                },
              ]}
              type="button"
              data-newsletter-image={issue.image}
              data-newsletter-title={issue.date}
              aria-label={`Open ${issue.date} newsletter`}
            >

              <div class="newsletter-masonry-item__visual">

                <img
                  src={issue.image}
                  alt={`${issue.date} Schneider Electric newsletter`}
                  loading="lazy"
                />

                <div class="newsletter-masonry-item__overlay">

                  <p class="newsletter-masonry-item__date">
                    {issue.date}
                  </p>

                  <div class="newsletter-masonry-item__stories">

                    {
                      issue.stories.map((story) => (
                        <span>{story}</span>
                      ))
                    }

                  </div>

                  <p class="newsletter-masonry-item__count">
                    {issue.stories.length}
                    {issue.stories.length === 1 ? ' story' : ' stories'}
                  </p>

                </div>

              </div>


              <div class="newsletter-masonry-item__caption">

                <span>{issue.date}</span>

                <i aria-hidden="true">
                  ↗
                </i>

              </div>

            </button>

          ))
        }

      </div>


          <!-- =====================================================
        2025
    ====================================================== -->

    <div class="newsletter-archive-year">

      <div class="newsletter-archive-year__heading">
        <span>01</span>

        <div>
          <p class="newsletter-kicker">
            Earlier editorial system
          </p>

          <h3 class="display">
            2025
          </h3>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div class="newsletter-masonry">

        {
          newsletterIssues2025.map((issue) => (

            <button
              class="newsletter-masonry-item"
              type="button"
              data-newsletter-image={issue.image}
              data-newsletter-title={issue.date}
              aria-label={`Open ${issue.date} newsletter`}
            >

              <div class="newsletter-masonry-item__visual">

                <img
                  src={issue.image}
                  alt={`${issue.date} Schneider Electric newsletter`}
                  loading="lazy"
                />

                <div class="newsletter-masonry-item__overlay">

                  <p class="newsletter-masonry-item__date">
                    {issue.date}
                  </p>

                  <div class="newsletter-masonry-item__stories">

                    {
                      issue.stories.map((story) => (
                        <span>{story}</span>
                      ))
                    }

                  </div>

                  <p class="newsletter-masonry-item__count">
                    {issue.stories.length}
                    {issue.stories.length === 1 ? ' story' : ' stories'}
                  </p>

                </div>

              </div>


              <div class="newsletter-masonry-item__caption">

                <span>{issue.date}</span>

                <i aria-hidden="true">
                  ↗
                </i>

              </div>

            </button>

          ))
        }

      </div>

    </div>


    </div>

  </section>



  <!-- =====================================================
      LIGHTBOX
  ====================================================== -->

  <div
    class="newsletter-lightbox"
    id="newsletter-lightbox"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >

    <button
      class="newsletter-lightbox__backdrop"
      type="button"
      aria-label="Close newsletter"
      data-lightbox-close
    ></button>


    <div
      class="newsletter-lightbox__dialog"
      role="dialog"
      aria-modal="true"
      aria-labelledby="newsletter-lightbox-title"
    >

      <div class="newsletter-lightbox__header">

        <p
          class="newsletter-lightbox__title"
          id="newsletter-lightbox-title"
        >
          Newsletter
        </p>

        <button
          class="newsletter-lightbox__close"
          type="button"
          aria-label="Close newsletter"
          data-lightbox-close
        >
          ×
        </button>

      </div>


      <div class="newsletter-lightbox__scroll">

        <img
          class="newsletter-lightbox__image"
          src=""
          alt=""
        />

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>



  <script>
    const lightbox = document.querySelector('#newsletter-lightbox');
    const lightboxImage =
      lightbox?.querySelector('.newsletter-lightbox__image');

    const lightboxTitle =
      lightbox?.querySelector('.newsletter-lightbox__title');

    const items =
      document.querySelectorAll('.newsletter-masonry-item');

    const closeButtons =
      lightbox?.querySelectorAll('[data-lightbox-close]');


    function openLightbox(item) {
      if (!lightbox || !lightboxImage || !lightboxTitle) return;

      const image = item.dataset.newsletterImage;
      const title = item.dataset.newsletterTitle;

      lightboxImage.src = image;
      lightboxImage.alt = `${title} newsletter`;
      lightboxTitle.textContent = title;

      lightbox.classList.add('is-open');
      lightbox.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');

      document.body.classList.add('newsletter-lightbox-open');
    }


    function closeLightbox() {
      if (!lightbox || !lightboxImage) return;

      lightbox.classList.remove('is-open');
      lightbox.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');

      document.body.classList.remove('newsletter-lightbox-open');

      setTimeout(() => {
        if (!lightbox.classList.contains('is-open')) {
          lightboxImage.src = '';
        }
      }, 250);
    }


    items.forEach((item) => {
      item.addEventListener('click', () => {
        openLightbox(item);
      });
    });


    closeButtons?.forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', closeLightbox);
    });


    document.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
      if (
        event.key === 'Escape' &&
        lightbox?.classList.contains('is-open')
      ) {
        closeLightbox();
      }
    });
  </script>


    <!-- =====================================================
         03 — EDITORIAL WORKFLOW
    ====================================================== -->

    <section class="newsletter-section shell">

      <div class="section-heading">

        <p class="eyebrow">
          Schneider Electric / Editorial Workflow
        </p>

        <div class="section-rule">
          <span>⌁</span>
        </div>

      </div>


      <div class="newsletter-section__intro">

        <h2 class="display">
          Activity to<br />
          <span>Narrative.</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          The format was recurring, but the content was not. Each edition
          required collecting, filtering and structuring a new set of inputs
          before the visual production stage began.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="newsletter-workflow">

        {
          workflow.map((step) => (

            <article>

              <span class="newsletter-workflow__number">
                {step.number}
              </span>

              <div>
                <h3>{step.label}</h3>
                <p>{step.text}</p>
              </div>

            </article>

          ))
