            I approached the CynLr newsletter problem as a perception-engineering exercise rather than a generic editorial task. The same pool of company stories was filtered through four stakeholder lenses — talent, investors, vendors and customers — based on what each audience needed to validate before engaging further.
          </p>
          <p class="cynlr-hero__intro">
            The work therefore began with the stakeholder question, not the available story: Do I want to build here? Can this scale? Where do we fit? Can this solve my problem? Content selection, sequencing, visual emphasis and calls to action were then shaped around that question.
          </p>

      </div>

